<BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Helvetica, sans-serif">quote:</font><HR>Killing Coldain is probably your quickest way to gain faction with Kael, since killing Coldain gives positive faction hits to both Kromzek AND Kromrif, and negative to both Coldain and DainFrostReaverIV. Killing in Skyshrine only gets you positive faction with Kromzek, and negative with ClawsofVeeshan and Yelinak. I think the positive faction hits on the dwarves in East Wastes are pretty good also. It has taken me about 16 hours at that camp to go from dubious to allied with Kromrif. It only took me about half that time to get to the point where I was safe to bank, but then, I was already allied to Kromzek when I started on the dwarves. From what I understand, the dorfs give a bigger hit for Kromrif, than they do for Kromzek, so killing in both places (Skyshrine and East Wastes) would probably be your best bet. And killing in skyshrine opens up the opportunity for armor and stuff. Killing coldain gets you nothing but faction, exp, and a little plat.<P><HR></BLOCKQUOTE>  <BR>By the time we get on I would bet that the courtyard is camped.<P>  Maybe it would be better to start with the dorfs so we start on a couple of diff. faction paths and get better faction faster.  Are we going to SS cause of the loot?  Just wondering.<P>Leaff<p>[ August 08, 2001: Message edited by: Hieck ]
